    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yes, indeed all good points and great that a tactic can at least have a shot of the overall global implications from the assumptions for each goal to the goal itself.</p>\n<p>Here is a <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mwe.html\">#mwe</a> for what I was illustrating above that is likely simpler to understand:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℕ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hab</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hcb</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">):</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∧</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∧</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">refine</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟨?_</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le_iff_eq_or_lt</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mpr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">?_</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">?_⟩</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"c1\">-- this will simplify the second goal but focus on it and &lt;;&gt; cannot simplify all goal any longer</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"c1\">-- &lt;;&gt; try left</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"c1\">-- this will simplify the second goal but focus on the two other goals and can never see the first goal any longer</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;;&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">first</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">left</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">skip</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"c1\">-- this does not discharge all three goals even though this simplification must apply to all of them</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;;&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">only</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">hab</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hcb</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"c1\">-- separate discharge of the skipped goal can happen here in some cases but not in others</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">exact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hab</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>What is particularly strange is that in the end I can't always discharge the dangling goal like in this example and trying something like admit/sorry would result in \"no goals to be closed\" while leaving it out will result in \"unsolved goals\" errors.</p>\n<p>Maybe there is still some easy enough tactic to close all three goals with a single <code>simp only [hab, hcb]</code> step? Or to reselect the dropped goals (middle goal dropped in first case and both other goals dropped in second case).</p>",
        "id": 607518979,
        "sender_full_name": "Plamen Dimitrov",
        "timestamp": 1782878449
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>4 messages were moved here from <a class=\"stream-topic\" data-stream-id=\"113489\" href=\"/#narrow/channel/113489-new-members/topic/Reusing.20goals.20to.20discharge.20others.20while.20proving.20in.20parallel/with/606158533\">#new members &gt; Reusing goals to discharge others while proving in parallel</a> by <span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"1100826\">lee gahyun</span>.</p>",
        "id": 607534486,
        "sender_full_name": "Notification Bot",
        "timestamp": 1782887845
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Ugh there's a bit of a mess where some messages are over at <a class=\"stream-topic\" data-stream-id=\"113489\" href=\"/#narrow/channel/113489-new-members/topic/Introduction.20and.20project.20feedback.20direction/with/607540332\">#new members &gt; Introduction and project feedback direction</a></p>",
        "id": 607621540,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1782914340
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"897334\">Plamen Dimitrov</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/113489-new-members/topic/Reusing.20goals.20to.20discharge.20others.20while.20proving.20in.20parallel/near/606158533\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I have a Lean 4 set of few goals where one goal overlaps with another, i.e. proving one goal will immediately prove the other goal. The goals look like</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"bp\">⊢</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">⊢</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">⊢</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∨</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>How can I eliminate the third goal and get just</p>\n<p><div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"bp\">⊢</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">⊢</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span>\n</code></pre></div><br>\n</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Try <code>refine ⟨?a, ?b, Or.inl ?a⟩</code> (untested)</p>",
        "id": 607628474,
        "sender_full_name": "Jz Pan",
        "timestamp": 1782916038
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"873547\">Robin Arnez</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/113489-new-members/topic/Reusing.20goals.20to.20discharge.20others.20while.20proving.20in.20parallel/near/607621540\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Ugh there's a bit of a mess where some messages are over at <a href=\"#narrow/channel/113489-new-members/topic/Introduction.20and.20project.20feedback.20direction/with/607540332\">new members &gt; Introduction and project feedback direction</a></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Indeed, the previous messages were already some valuable feedback, <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"1100826\">@lee gahyun</span> could you restore the messages in this thread?</p>",
        "id": 607748863,
        "sender_full_name": "Plamen Dimitrov",
        "timestamp": 1782965504
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"366779\">Jz Pan</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/113489-new-members/topic/Reusing.20goals.20to.20discharge.20others.20while.20proving.20in.20parallel/near/607628474\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"897334\">Plamen Dimitrov</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/113489-new-members/topic/Reusing.20goals.20to.20discharge.20others.20while.20proving.20in.20parallel/near/606158533\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I have a Lean 4 set of few goals where one goal overlaps with another, i.e. proving one goal will immediately prove the other goal. The goals look like</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"bp\">⊢</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">⊢</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">⊢</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∨</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>How can I eliminate the third goal and get just</p>\n<p><div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"bp\">⊢</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">⊢</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span>\n</code></pre></div><br>\n</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Try <code>refine ⟨?a, ?b, Or.inl ?a⟩</code> (untested)</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>This has some upfront limitations like:</p>\n<p>1) It doesn't handle nested pattern matching like <code>refine ⟨⟨h1, h2, h3, ?_, ?_⟩, ?c⟩</code> and can only name the top level goals.<br>\n2) It cannot handle in-line simplifications like the <code>le_iff_eq_or_lt</code> written within the refine line.</p>\n<p>but both of these can be done with extra preceding simplification steps but there might be some cases out there where one would need to work on one goal first to simplify it enough (in a way that is not possible to be done on all conjoined goals in advance) to then discharge it via another already set goal.</p>\n<p>So in my case I would have considered tactics like <code>first</code> and <code>try</code> + goal selection to give me more refined control over this process. They sort of did but you can see some very unnatural behaviors above (comments in the example starting with <code>-- this ...</code> that I might even consider bugs.</p>",
        "id": 607754456,
        "sender_full_name": "Plamen Dimitrov",
        "timestamp": 1782968777
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>You can introduce a proof of <code>A</code> using <code>have</code> before splitting goals, and then use it in different places.</p>",
        "id": 607755506,
        "sender_full_name": "Etienne Marion",
        "timestamp": 1782969476
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"703970\">Etienne Marion</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/113489-new-members/topic/Reusing.20goals.20to.20discharge.20others.20while.20proving.20in.20parallel/near/607755506\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>You can introduce a proof of <code>A</code> using <code>have</code> before splitting goals, and then use it in different places.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Yes but my main point is about this:</p>\n<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"897334\">Plamen Dimitrov</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/113489-new-members/topic/Reusing.20goals.20to.20discharge.20others.20while.20proving.20in.20parallel/near/607754456\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>So in my case I would have considered tactics like <code>first</code> and <code>try</code> + goal selection to give me more refined control over this process. They sort of did but you can see some very unnatural behaviors above (comments in the example starting with <code>-- this ...</code> that I might even consider bugs.</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 608159203,
        "sender_full_name": "Plamen Dimitrov",
        "timestamp": 1783136302
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The reason your <code>try</code> / <code>first</code> sequences don't work is that <code>&lt;;&gt;</code> binds stronger than you might expect. When you write</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">refine</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟨?_</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le_iff_eq_or_lt</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mpr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">?_</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">?_⟩</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">&lt;;&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">first</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">left</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">skip</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">&lt;;&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">only</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">hab</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hcb</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Lean interprets it as</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">refine</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟨?_</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le_iff_eq_or_lt</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mpr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">?_</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">?_⟩</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">&lt;;&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">first</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">left</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">skip</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;;&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">only</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">hab</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hcb</span><span class=\"o\">])</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Therefore, <code>simp only</code> is only executed on the <code>skip</code> branches (1st &amp; 3rd goal). The same goes for <code>try</code>, where <code>try tac &lt;;&gt; tac</code> is <code>try (tac &lt;;&gt; tac)</code>.</p>\n<p>You might want to fix associativity with explicit parenthesis:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">refine</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟨?_</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le_iff_eq_or_lt</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mpr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">?_</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">?_⟩</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">&lt;;&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">try</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">left</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">&lt;;&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">assumption</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Or use binder tactics in the place of <code>&lt;;&gt;</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">refine</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟨?_</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le_iff_eq_or_lt</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mpr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">?_</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">?_⟩</span>\n<span class=\"n\">any_goals</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">left</span>\n<span class=\"n\">all_goals</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">assumption</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 608253838,
        "sender_full_name": "fnHoj",
        "timestamp": 1783229644
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Thanks <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"970781\">@fnHoj</span>, your reply here really gets into the crux of the problem. Awesome!</p>",
